# p3_a1r. Every target has a glass block above it (Serene Seasons skips covered blocks, p3_a1r P3-RC).
pace 1

## SQ-MELT-06b | part 2: vanillaLightMelting true: ice touching a sea lantern melts (vanilla light melt back)
shell grep -nE "vanillaLightMelting" config/creativecommon-common.toml
bootexpect \[melting\] tags:
> pbot spawn m3 2060 -60 2060 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot spawn m3r 2210 -60 2060 minecraft:overworld survival
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> setblock 2091 -61 2120 minecraft:ice
> setblock 2090 -61 2120 minecraft:sea_lantern
> setblock 2091 -60 2120 minecraft:glass
> zmelt w m06b_sl_ice1 overworld 2091 -61 2120
> zmelt w m06_sealantern_ice1 overworld 2241 -61 2072
> zmelt w m06_redstonetorch_ice1 overworld 2241 -61 2084
> zmelt light overworld 2091 -61 2120
sleep 2
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 1000
sleep 90
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> zmelt show
waitlog \[zmelt\] show done 30
> execute if block 2091 -61 2120 minecraft:water run say SQ-MELT-06b-new_sl_ice_water
> execute if block 2241 -61 2072 minecraft:water run say SQ-MELT-06b-old_sl_ice_water
> execute if block 2241 -61 2084 minecraft:ice run say SQ-MELT-06b-redstonetorch_ice_kept
expect SQ-MELT-06b-new_sl_ice_water$
expect SQ-MELT-06b-old_sl_ice_water$
look redstone torch (light 7, under vanilla's 11) keeps its ice with the switch on too
